3,"El Wali - 10 of May (from Tiris) - YouTube‘This music survived in a network of phones’: El Wali, the ...El Wali (band) - WikipediaTiris | El Wali‘This music survived in a network of phones’: El Wali,…El Wali - Tiris – Sahel Sounds",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mYX9AG_pYB8,"Dec 9, 2019 · One of the first Saharan music to incorporate the electric guitar, the style was hugely influential on the better know Tuareg guitar genre. The later addition of synthesizer and programmed... Mar 14, 2024 · The concept is clear: everything is El Wali when it comes to Polisario music. Some members stay in the band longer than others, but there have been so many that each camp has certainly provided more than one. The band's music first appeared anonymously as ""Polisario"" on a 2012 compilation from the Sahel Sounds label, Music from Saharan Cellphones, before Tiris was released in 2019. The later addition of synthesizer and programmed rhythms further transformed the sound, becoming a foundation of Sahrawi music. Recorded in Belgium in 1994 while on tour, this version of El Wali performed a style reflecting the popular music of the refugee camps. Mar 13, 2024 · Around 2009, Kirkley was touring the Sahel (a stretch of the southern Sahara) and west Africa to collect samples of local music for an album series called Music from Saharan Cellphones. Recorded in Belgium in 1994 while on tour, this version of El Wali performed a style reflecting the popular music of the refugee camps. “Tiris” is a refreshing production with none of the typical World Music polish of the 90s.",Wali,Nilo-Saharan
